Qwen3.8-27B on TensorFold v0.6.5: video input and larger media limits. Ported from patch
0001-qwen27-many-images-video.patch of the Qwen3.8-27B-DGX-Spark-TensorFold recipe (against v0.6.0, Apache-2.0, a
modification of TensorFold by the TensorFold contributors; its video code was MiaAI-Lab's Flash Next patch). v0.6.5
ships that video code and the many-images flags (--vision-max-images, --vision-image-tokens, TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_TOKENS)
itself but turns video on only for Flash Next (qwen4_exp); this turns it on for the 27B (qwen3_5) too. The size limits
become environment variables whose defaults are v0.6.5's: TENSORFOLD_REQUEST_BODY_MIB (32), TENSORFOLD_IMAGE_TOTAL_MIB
(20, all of a request's images), TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_MIB (16, one video), TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_TOTAL_MIB (20).
Applies after 0001.

